# UCUM functional tests

`UcumFunctionalTests.xml` is the UCUM conformance suite, copied unchanged from
the FHIR Java implementation of UCUM
(https://github.com/FHIR/Ucum-java/blob/master/src/test/resources/UcumFunctionalTests.xml,
fetched 2026-10-11; its last history entry is dated 3 February 2021).

Licensing: the file's own header states that it is copyright 2008-2009 Grahame
Grieve and contributors and licensed under the Eclipse Public License
(http://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-v10.html). The repository it ships in is
licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License, reproduced in `LICENSE` beside it.

`TestUCUMFunctionalSuite` (internal/vocabulary/ucum_test.go) runs its
validation and conversion cases against the substrate's unit grammar. A case
over an atom the unit table does not carry is skipped and counted, never
passed.

# UCUM atom codes

`atoms.tsv` lists every case-sensitive atom code in UCUM 2.2's
`ucum-essence.xml` (revision date 2024-06-17), with whether UCUM marks it
metric. It was extracted from
https://github.com/ucum-org/ucum/blob/main/ucum-essence.xml, fetched
2026-10-11: the `Code` attribute of every `base-unit` element (all metric) and
of every `unit` element, with its `isMetric` attribute. The functional suite
above names no such inventory, and it never writes `st`, the stere.

Licensing: UCUM is copyright 1999-2024 Regenstrief Institute, Inc., and the
list is used under the UCUM License, Version 1.1
(https://unitsofmeasure.org/license), whose notice heads the file.

`TestUnitAliasesSpellNoUCUMCode` (internal/vocabulary/ucumatoms_test.go)
refuses an input alias that reads as a UCUM expression over these atoms,
including the ones the unit table does not carry yet.
